# Payment System Flow



## 1: Client Hires a Contractor
Tasks:
* UX: Client views proposals.
* UX: Client clicks “Hire”.
* UX: Client sets contract terms.
* UX: Client chooses a payment method.
* API: POST /contracts – Link freelancer, job, and client. (update backend and db)
* API: POST /contracts – Store contract terms. (update backend and db)
* API: POST /payments/setup – Validate payment method (card, PayPal, etc.)
* API: POST /payments/setup – Initiate escrow for fixed-price contracts  
## 2: Escrow System Integration
Tasks:
* API: POST /escrow/deposit
*  - Charge client’s funding source.
*  - Create escrow wallet entry.
*  - Confirm funds held securely.
* API: GET /escrow/balance – Retrieve funding status for contract.

## 3: Freelancer Submits Work
Tasks:
* UX: Freelancer submits milestone or deliverables for hourly or retainers.
*  – Notify client of delivery (
* Start 5/7/14-day escrow countdown timer 
## 4: Client Approves Work and Releases Payment
Tasks:
* UX: Client reviews submitted work.
* UX: Client clicks “Approve & Release Payment”.
* API: POST /escrow/release – Transfer funds to freelancer’s Upwork wallet. (admin approves pending transaction??)
* API: POST /escrow/release – Trigger email/notification to freelancer.
* API: POST /transaction – Record transaction to ledger. 
* API: POST /transaction – Deduct platform service fee (10% ??)

## 5: Freelancer Withdraws Payment
Tasks:
* UX: Freelancer checks pending/available balance.
* UX: Freelancer clicks “Get Paid”.
* UX: Selects payout method (bank, PayPal, Payoneer).
* API: GET /wallet – Retrieve pending and available balances.
* API: POST /payouts/initiate – Validate and initiate withdrawal.
* API: POST /payouts/initiate – Create ledger entry and process external transfer.

## 6: Contract Completion and Feedback
Tasks:
* UX: Client ends contract.
* UX: Both parties submit rating.
*  Contract marked as completed.